Let Last.fm stand in while ListenBrainz rate-limits popularity reads.

Why: the discover page lets Last.fm stand in for ListenBrainz popularity
only when ListenBrainz switches the endpoint off (its "disabled" 500 and
anti-scraper 401). A 429 does not count, so every build keeps asking: a
background read gets three attempts in up to 30 s, longer than the 25 s
bound on each shelf, and Top Picks, Daily Mixes and Missing Essentials time
out empty on every build. Measured 2026-10-25 on music.xarif.de: the
MetaBrainz gateway answered every ListenBrainz call with a 429 that carries
none of ListenBrainz's X-RateLimit headers (x-mb-gateway: rudi), and three
builds in a row (14:53, 14:57, 15:05 UTC) left those three shelves empty
while Last.fm answered 22 of 22 calls. A popularity read turned down for
its rate now marks popularity down like a refusal: for the wait the 429
names, else for the refusal window (10 minutes). The build stops asking,
Last.fm stands in when the user has it, and ListenBrainz gets fewer calls
while it is limiting. A 503 still leaves popularity up.

Tests: unit tests for the down window (refusal, rate limit with and
without a named wait, 503). The two rate-limit tests fail without the
change. droppedneedle-catalog lib and the catalog integration suite
(symlink-free TMPDIR): same single failure with and without the patch
(reads_artwork::a_compat_cover_joins_a_running_fetch).

Remove when: upstream lets a rate-limited ListenBrainz hand popularity to
Last.fm.

